  "id": "theta-wave",
  "term": "theta wave",
  "definition": "A theta wave is an electroencephalographic brain-wave activity pattern discussed here in the roughly 6–9 Hz range as part of a theta/alpha component. In this source, increased theta activity in anterior brain regions was reported in chronic schizophrenia, making it relevant as a possible diagnostic biomarker.",
